I go near the main door.
There is a large wooden counter there.
An elderly man is sitting behind the counter.
There is a cash register in front of him.
I stop near the counter.
"Hello, chacha," I say respectfully.
Chacha looks at me.
He smiles very warmly.
"Hello, madam," he says.
There is a large glass on the counter.
There is a menu under the glass.
It is a handwritten menu.
I read the menu carefully.
It has the names of many items.
"Do you need something, madam?" chacha asks.
I look at him and smile.
"Yes, I just need a minute," I say.
I look for something good in the menu.
